# The residual 17-generator Held Schreier problem

These are the 49 short words used by the retained 168-coset discovery trace.
They are syntactic data, not asserted relations of Held's presentation.
`ReducedEnumeration` proves a conditional membership theorem for any group
satisfying them. Connecting them to the source presentation is a separate proof
obligation. Original labels refer to the Schreier spanning tree rooted at ATLAS
point 1206, using the source right action and right-conjugation convention.

Source: John Bray, ATLAS `HeG1-P1.M`, retained in `Held/Model/Source/`.
The data were discovered by GAP Tietze transformations and Felsch enumeration;
only the emitted Lean proofs give mathematical evidence.
-/

